.TH FASTRDP-TERMSRV-CHECK 8 "October 2026" "fast-rdp-server" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
fastrdp-termsrv-check \- check that a keytab has AES keys for the TERMSRV principals
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B fastrdp-termsrv-check
.RB [ \-k
.IR keytab ]
.I principal ...
.SH DESCRIPTION
FreeRDP's Kerberos acceptor (the fastrdp proxy) cannot use RC4 session keys.
.B fastrdp-termsrv-check
reads the keytab with
.B klist \-ke
and checks, for every
.IR principal ,
that it has an AES key (aes256- or aes128-cts-hmac-sha1-96) at its newest key
version number. A principal without
.BI @ REALM
matches any realm; names compare case-insensitively. It prints one
.B ok
or
.B FAIL
line per principal and, on failure, how to fix the account.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-k " keytab"
Keytab to check. Default: FASTRDP_TERMSRV_KEYTAB from the environment or from
.IR /etc/fastrdp/termsrv.conf ,
else
.IR /etc/fastrdp/termsrv.keytab .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.B FASTRDP_TERMSRV_CONF
names another configuration file.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 all principals ok, 1 a principal is missing or has no AES key (or the
keytab is unreadable), 2 usage.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
fastrdp-termsrv-check TERMSRV/rdp1.example.com TERMSRV/RDP1
fastrdp-termsrv-check \-k /etc/krb5.keytab TERMSRV/rdp1.example.com
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fastrdp-termsrv-keytab (8),
.BR klist (1)
